{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     unit — one row in a curriculum list, on NSDS's .ns-unit.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     PARAMETERS
       currentSlug   slug of the page being viewed, so the row can mark
                     itself. Passed in rather than reached for: inside a
                     {{#get}} → {{#foreach}} the path back to the post is a
                     stack of `../` that changes the moment the nesting does.

     `data-state` is an attribute, not a class — this system's rule, and here
     it also means the CSS and the screen reader read one fact.

     ONLY TWO STATES ARE HONEST. Ghost has no per-member progress, so it
     cannot know whether a reader has COMPLETED a lesson. "You are here" and
     "not yet" are the two it can know; drawing a tick against the others
     would be telling the reader something the site does not know.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<a class="ns-unit" href="{{url}}"
   data-state="{{#match slug currentSlug}}current{{else}}todo{{/match}}"
   {{#match slug currentSlug}}aria-current="page"{{/match}}>
    <span class="ns-unit__title">{{title}}</span>
    <span class="ns-unit__type sp-optional">{{~> "internal/format"~}}</span>
    <span class="ns-unit__time sp-duration sp-optional">{{~> "internal/duration"~}}</span>
</a>
